        "title": "CapLite: Prompt-Injection Defense for Small Language Model Agents without Model-Written Security Artifacts",
        "source": "arXiv",
        "summary": "Enforcement defenses against prompt injection, such as CaMeL, Progent, IPIGuard and DRIFT, ask the agent's own model to write a security artifact (a program, a privilege policy, a dependency graph or a constraint list) that code then enforces. We ask whether small language model (SLM) agents can be trusted to write these artifacts. Across 15 open-weight models, 13 of them between 1.7B and 12B parameters, they cannot: the policies, graphs and cons",
